 "stimulus_html": "Perform the following operations without a calculator. Simplify if possible.",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 505356,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"84\\sqrt {132}  \\div \\left(14\\sqrt {11} \\right)\">84\\sqrt {132}  \\div \\left(14\\sqrt {11}\\right)</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"84\\sqrt {132}  \\div \\left( {14\\sqrt {11} } \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Divide the rational part.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"84 \\div 14 = 6\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: If necessary, reduce the result of Step 1 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p>Not necessary.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Divide the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {132{\\rm{ }}}  \\div {\\rm{ }}\\sqrt {11} {\\rm{ }} = {\\rm{ }}\\sqrt {12} \"></span></p>\n<p>Step 4: If necessary, reduce the result from Step 3 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {12}  = \\sqrt 4 \\sqrt 3  = 2\\sqrt 3 \"></span></p>\n<p>Step 5: The result is the product of the rational and the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"6\\left( {2\\sqrt 3 } \\right) = 12\\sqrt 3 \"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"12\\sqrt 3\">12\\sqrt 3</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 505357,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<span data-math=\"57\\sqrt {792}  \\div \\left(25\\sqrt {2}\\right)\">57\\sqrt {792}  \\div \\left(25\\sqrt {2}\\right)</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p><span data-math=\"57\\sqrt {792}  \\div \\left( {25\\sqrt 2 } \\right)\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 1: Divide the rational part.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"57 \\div 25 = \\frac{{57}}{{25}}\"></span></p>\n<p>Step 2: If necessary, reduce the result of Step 1 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p>Not necessary.</p>\n<p>Step 3: Divide the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {792}  \\div {\\rm{ }}\\sqrt 2 {\\rm{ }} = {\\rm{ }}\\sqrt {\\frac{{792}}{2}}  = \\sqrt {396} \"></span></p>\n<p>Step 4: If necessary, reduce the result from Step 3 to lowest terms.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\sqrt {396}  = \\sqrt {36} \\sqrt {11}  = 6\\sqrt {11} \"></span></p>\n<p>Step 5: The result is the product of the rational and the irrational parts.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\frac{{57}}{{25}}\\left( {6\\sqrt {11} } \\right) = \\frac{{342}}{{25}}\\sqrt {11} \"></span></p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<span data-math=\"\\frac{{342}}{{25}}\\sqrt {11}\">\\frac{{342}}{{25}}\\sqrt {11}</span>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
